        {
          "title": "Apply Bayes' theorem",
          "body": "$$P(F \\mid HH) = \\frac{P(F)\\,P(HH \\mid F)}{P(HH)} = \\frac{1/5}{2/5} = \\frac12 = 0.50$$\n\nBoth branches contribute the same $\\frac15$, so given HH the two explanations are equally likely.",
